{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md | sed -n '20,199p'\"","aggregated_output":"    20\t**Scope**\n    21\t\n    22\tIn:\n    23\t\n    24\t- `archiveEntries` Convex append/read functions\n    25\t- Atomic sequence assignment per process\n    26\t- `processId + finalizationKey` idempotency guard\n    27\t- Required archive entry kind validation\n    28\t- Rejection of unsupported archive entry kinds\n    29\t- Stable ascending read order using `sequence`\n    30\t- Same-timestamp deterministic ordering through sequence\n    31\t- Optional related artifact, source provenance, and tool correlation ids\n    32\t- Basic archive-entry page shape returned from store methods\n    33\t\n    34\tOut:\n    35\t\n    36\t- Live finalization hook behavior, owned by Story 2\n    37\t- Browser/user-facing archive read routes and UI, owned by Story 3\n    38\t- Read-time provenance enrichment, owned by Story 6\n    39\t- Turn and derived-view records\n    40\t- Historical migration/backfill\n    41\t\n    42\t**Dependencies**\n    43\t\n    44\t- Story 0 foundation\n    45\t- `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md` before Convex implementation\n    46\t- [tech-design.md](../tech-design.md)\n    47\t- [test-plan.md](../test-plan.md)\n    48\t\n    49\t### Acceptance Criteria\n    50\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\n    51\t**AC-1.1:** The canonical archive-entry primitive persists finalized low-level entries supplied by trusted callers.\n    52\t\n    53\t- **TC-1.1a: User message entry appended through primitive**\n    54\t  - Given: A trusted caller submits a finalized `user_message` payload for one process\n    55\t  - When: The archive-entry append primitive is invoked\n    56\t  - Then: A canonical `user_message` archive entry is persisted for that process\n    57\t- **TC-1.1b: Model message entry appended through primitive**\n    58\t  - Given: A trusted caller submits a finalized `model_message` payload for one process\n    59\t  - When: The archive-entry append primitive is invoked\n    60\t  - Then: A canonical `model_message` archive entry is persisted for that process\n    61\t- **TC-1.1c: Process event entry appended through primitive**\n    62\t  - Given: A trusted caller submits a finalized `process_event` payload for one process\n    63\t  - When: The archive-entry append primitive is invoked\n    64\t  - Then: A canonical `process_event` archive entry is persisted for that process\n    65\t\n    66\t**AC-1.2:** The canonical archive supports the PRD entry taxonomy.\n    67\t\n    68\t- **TC-1.2a: Required archive entry kinds accepted**\n    69\t  - Given: The platform appends finalized archive entries\n    70\t  - When: Each required entry kind is recorded\n    71\t  - Then: The archive accepts `user_message`, `model_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, and `process_event`\n    72\t- **TC-1.2b: Unsupported archive entry kind rejected**\n    73\t  - Given: A caller attempts to append an unsupported archive entry kind\n    74\t  - When: The append request is validated\n    75\t  - Then: The platform rejects the entry and does not append a partial archive record\n    76\t\n    77\t**AC-1.3:** Archive entries preserve order within one process.\n    78\t\n    79\t- **TC-1.3a: Process archive entries read in stable order**\n    80\t  - Given: Multiple archive entries exist for one process\n    81\t  - When: The archive is read in ascending order\n    82\t  - Then: Entries appear in their canonical process order\n    83\t- **TC-1.3b: Same-timestamp entries remain deterministic**\n    84\t  - Given: Multiple archive entries have the same timestamp\n    85\t  - When: The archive is read\n    86\t  - Then: The platform returns them in a stable deterministic order\n    87\t\n    88\t**AC-1.4:** Archive entries can store and return related process, artifact, source, or tool ids without depending on read-time enrichment.\n    89\t\n    90\t- **TC-1.4a: Related ids round-trip through archive storage**\n    91\t  - Given: An archive entry includes related artifact, source provenance, or tool correlation ids\n    92\t  - When: The archive entry is appended and later read through the primitive\n    93\t  - Then: The stored related ids are returned unchanged on the canonical archive row\n    94\t- **TC-1.4b: Archive row remains readable without related-record lookup**\n    95\t  - Given: An archive entry stores nullable related ids and no related-record enrichment is performed\n    96\t  - When: The archive entry is read through the primitive\n    97\t  - Then: The canonical archive row remains readable without requiring artifact or source resolution\n    98\t\n    99\t### Technical Design\n   100\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\n   101\tThis story owns only the durable canonical archive-entry primitive.\n   102\t\n   103\t#### Architecture Context\n   104\t\n   105\tStory 1 creates the archive domain’s durable append/read primitive. Fastify and\n   106\tlater services decide when something is finalized enough to archive, but this\n   107\tstory owns the canonical row shape, per-process ordering, and idempotent append\n   108\tcontract that the rest of Epic 7 builds on.\n   109\t\n   110\t#### Convex Tables and Indexes\n   111\t\n   112\t| Table | Responsibility |\n   113\t|---|---|\n   114\t| `archiveEntries` | Canonical finalized low-level archive entries |\n   115\t\n   116\t| Index | Fields | Purpose |\n   117\t|---|---|---|\n   118\t| `by_processId_sequence` | `processId`, `sequence` | Canonical archive pagination and stable ordering |\n   119\t| `by_processId_finalizationKey` | `processId`, `finalizationKey` | Idempotency guard |\n   120\t| `by_projectId_processId_recordedAt` | `projectId`, `processId`, `recordedAt` | Project/process scoped diagnostics |\n   121\t\n   122\t#### PlatformStore Methods\n   123\t\n   124\t| Method | Description |\n   125\t|---|---|\n   126\t| `appendArchiveEntry(args)` | Appends one finalized canonical entry or returns/no-ops an existing entry for the same process/finalization key |\n   127\t| `listArchiveEntries(args)` | Returns one bounded page sorted by ascending `sequence` |\n   128\t\n   129\t#### Implementation Targets\n   130\t\n   131\t| Area | Files / Modules |\n   132\t|------|-----------------|\n   133\t| Durable archive storage | `convex/archiveEntries.ts`, `convex/schema.ts` |\n   134\t| Store seam | `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts` |\n   135\t| Shared archive contract consumption | `apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts` |\n   136\t\n   137\tImplementation notes:\n   138\t\n   139\t- Convex assigns `sequence` inside the append mutation. Fastify may preflight finalization keys, but Convex owns the atomic guard.\n   140\t- The append mutation validates the seven-entry taxonomy and rejects unsupported kinds without persisting partial rows.\n   141\t- `lifecycleState` is always `finalized`.\n   142\t- `finalizationKey` is unique within a process and stable across retries.\n   143\t- Same-timestamp ordering is deterministic because reads sort by `sequence`, not `recordedAt`.\n   144\t- Related ids are nullable and round-trip as stored values on the canonical row.\n   145\t- Missing related records do not delete or hide the archive row.\n   146\t- Service-level finalization proof is completed in Story 2.\n   147\t- Full artifact/source enrichment and related-record lookup degradation are completed in Story 6.\n   148\t\n   149\t#### Design References\n   150\t\n   151\t- [tech-design.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:139), lines 139-149\n   152\t- [tech-design.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:223), lines 223-271\n   153\t- [tech-design.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:563), lines 563-585\n   154\t- [test-plan.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:36), lines 36-44\n   155\t\n   156\t#### Test Mapping\n   157\t\n   158\t| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\n   159\t|----|-------------------|------------------|\n   160\t| TC-1.1a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | appends finalized `user_message` entry through primitive |\n   161\t| TC-1.1b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | appends finalized `model_message` entry through primitive |\n   162\t| TC-1.1c | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | appends finalized `process_event` entry through primitive |\n   163\t| TC-1.2a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | accepts required archive entry kinds |\n   164\t| TC-1.2b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | rejects unsupported archive entry kind |\n   165\t| TC-1.3a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | reads entries in stable sequence order |\n   166\t| TC-1.3b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | same timestamp entries remain deterministic |\n   167\t| TC-1.4a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | round-trips related artifact/source/tool ids |\n   168\t| TC-1.4b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | reads archive row without requiring related-record lookup |\n   169\t\n   170\t#### Non-TC Decided Tests\n   171\t\n   172\t- `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts`: sequence assignment is atomic across same-process appends\n   173\t- `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts`: same `processId + finalizationKey` returns or no-ops an existing archive row\n   174\t\n   175\t#### Technical Notes\n   176\t\n   177\t- This story owns durable append/read primitives only. It does not decide when an object is final enough to append, and it does not prove service-level finalization hooks or read-time provenance enrichment.\n   178\t\n   179\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\n   180\t\n   181\t- Prove stable order and idempotency through the real persistence boundary, not by sorting mock arrays in a unit helper.\n   182\t\n   183\t#### Verification\n   184\t\n   185\t- Targeted: `pnpm run test:convex`\n   186\t- Story gate: `pnpm run green-verify`\n   187\t- Epic gate: `pnpm run verify-all`\n   188\t\n   189\t#### Spec Deviations\n   190\t\n   191\tNone.\n   192\t\n   193\tSee the tech design document for full architecture, implementation targets, and test mapping.\n   194\t\n   195\t### Definition of Done\n   196\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\n   197\t- `archiveEntries` durable functions append and read finalized entries\n   198\t- All required archive entry kinds are accepted; unsupported kinds are rejected without partial persistence\n   199\t- Sequence assignment is stable, per-process, and deterministic for same-timestamp entries\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
